    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Mimir-Prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Span ingest volume at the collector's OTLP receiver, with the refused counter on the same axis for scale. This is the DENOMINATOR that makes a flat 0 refused readable: without it, 0 refused looks identical whether the collector is healthy or receiving nothing at all. A drop to 0 accepted with 0 refused means the producers stopped, not that ingest is clean.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23
      },
      "id": 8,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Mimir-Prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(otelcol_receiver_accepted_spans_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "accepted",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Mimir-Prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(otelcol_receiver_refused_spans_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "refused",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Span ingest volume (accepted vs refused)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Mimir-Prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Metric-point and log-record ingest volume, split BY RECEIVER on purpose. The self-scrape receiver (prometheus/internal) and hostmetrics together dominate the metric-point total, so a single sum() hides the application plane. Only the otlp series is application metrics. If your deployment gates application metrics to a subset of environments, a low otlp figure is expected there, not a defect. Likewise, if your applications ship logs to a platform log service rather than through this collector, a thin log-record line is expected.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 23
      },
      "id": 9,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Mimir-Prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(otelcol_receiver_accepted_metric_points_total[5m])) by (receiver)",
          "legendFormat": "accepted {{receiver}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Mimir-Prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(otelcol_receiver_refused_metric_points_total[5m])) by (receiver)",
          "legendFormat": "refused {{receiver}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
